WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.740
Night in a trench.

2
00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:03.410
Snow is falling.

3
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:08.170
The wire shakes in the wind,
and a flare drifts slowly down.

4
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:13.235
The men keep watch: "Wearied we keep
awake because the night is silent .

5
00:00:13.285 --> 00:00:13.578
.

6
00:00:13.628 --> 00:00:13.920
."

7
00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:17.420
Night turns to dawn,
and dawn to night again.

8
00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:20.400
And each time: "But nothing happens."

9
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:21.360
No battle.

10
00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:22.550
No attack.

11
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.370
So what is killing these soldiers?

12
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.830
In this mission, you'll meet Wilfred Owen,

13
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:32.330
who served in France from December 1916,
and wrote from his own winter at the

14
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.410
front.

15
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.450
You'll trace the poem's
slow, repeating shape:

16
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.200
stanzas that never seem to get anywhere.

17
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:42.200
And you'll weigh every
suspect the poem lines up:

18
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.790
bullets, wind, snow, and the waiting.

19
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.570
Your mission: work out what
is killing these soldiers.
